###
### The secrets store for cts-fvt's two servers, named by the "ctsFvtSecretsStore" placeholder variable in
### this module's application.properties.
###
### Both servers are configured with a secrets store deliberately, and this harness is the only FVT suite
### where that store is actually read.  When a server has one, OMRSEnterpriseConnectorManager builds a
### secrets store connection for the REST_BEARER_TOKEN purpose and embeds it in every remote cohort
### member's connection before asking the connector broker for a connector - so this file is on the path
### the workbench takes to reach the technology under test, and it is the path a defect was once found on
### (see this module's README).  Configuring a store that does not exist would leave that path only
### half-exercised, and logs YAML-SECRETS-STORE-CONNECTOR-0001 once per registration attempt.
###
### The collection below deliberately supplies no token and no tokenAPI.  The platform this harness starts
### has no user directory and CtsFvtSecurityConfig installs a permit-all filter chain, so there is nothing
### to authenticate to and no token endpoint to fetch a token from.  With no "token" secret the REST client
### connector finds none, sets no authorization header, and calls the other server unauthenticated - which
### is what this platform expects.  A tokenAPI here would only add a call to a token endpoint that is not
### running.
###

secretsCollections:
    cts-fvt:
        displayName: cts-fvt servers
        description: >
            Secrets for the two servers the cts-fvt conformance suite harness stands up.  Intentionally
            empty of secrets - the harness's platform authenticates no one.
        refreshTimeInterval: 3600
